# The checks of the C++ tests: the package's, less two. A test's numbers are
# the amounts, dates, and counts its claims name, so they are not magic; and a
# test reads an optional it expects present with value(), whose exception the
# runner reports as the test's failure, rather than checking it first.
InheritParentConfig: true
Checks: >
  -bugprone-unchecked-optional-access,
  -cppcoreguidelines-avoid-magic-numbers,
  -readability-magic-numbers
